  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 3NT. South only has 6 top tricks (the ♠A, 4 heart tricks, and the ♣A). South can develop 1 or 2 extra trick in clubs. Even if the club finesse is working, South will still have to play on diamonds to come to enough tricks.\n\nThe diamond suit will provide enough tricks for the contract regardless of who has the ♣K. South should hold up the ♠A for three rounds to exhaust East of his spades in case that suit is 5-3 and East has the ♦A. If West has 5 spades and the ♦A the contract has no hope even if East has the ♣K.\n\nSouth now knocks out the ♦A. If East wins the ♦A and returns a club, South should rise with the ♣A and cash his 9 tricks.\n\nThe contract would still be secure if the defensive spades were divided 4-4. In this case, East would still have a spade left upon winning the ♦A but the defense would only have 4 tricks available. The contract would be safe without risking the club finesse.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠K against 3NT. South only has 6 top tricks (the ♠A, 4 heart tricks, and the ♣A). South can develop 1 or 2 extra trick in clubs. Even if the club finesse is working, South will still have to play on diamonds to come to enough tricks.",
    "The diamond suit will provide enough tricks for the contract regardless of who has the ♣K. South should hold up the ♠A for three rounds to exhaust East of his spades in case that suit is 5-3 and East has the ♦A. If West has 5 spades and the ♦A the contract has no hope even if East has the ♣K.",
    "South now knocks out the ♦A. If East wins the ♦A and returns a club, South should rise with the ♣A and cash his 9 tricks.",
    "The contract would still be secure if the defensive spades were divided 4-4. In this case, East would still have a spade left upon winning the ♦A but the defense would only have 4 tricks available. The contract would be safe without risking the club finesse."
